From fe37e86471436256b42fbcf9a77fe31887b2a83b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AF9 <af9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:58:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Auxiliary power: energy hatches switch between Primary
 and Auxiliary, multiblocks draw auxiliary power for the recipes that ask for
 it

- EnergyHatchPartMachine: an input hatch has a power mode (screwdriver). Auxiliary hatches are no recipe handlers: the
  machine's recipes do not draw on them.
- WorkableMultiblockMachine: a recipe's data af9_aux_eut (EU/t) is drawn from the auxiliary hatches while it runs and has
  to be there to start; a machine can add a base demand (getBaseAuxiliaryEUt). The handlers are collected again when a
  hatch changes its mode.
- Power Management: a side tab on every multiblock's screen with the primary and the auxiliary power.
- The recipe viewers' EU line says the auxiliary power in its tooltip.
Version 7.5.3-af9.4.
